1
00:00:01,679 --> 00:00:03,681
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,981
GOTTA BUY A STEP STOOL

3
00:01:36,065 --> 00:01:37,566
{\an8}Here's pepper spray.

4
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:41,779
{\an8}You just aim it at their face and try
to get as much as you can in their eyes.

5
00:01:41,862 --> 00:01:43,405
Okay? Definitely stings.

6
00:01:43,489 --> 00:01:44,490
[Haru laughs] All right.

7
00:01:44,573 --> 00:01:46,408
This is a really loud siren.

8
00:01:46,492 --> 00:01:48,619
You want the sound to reach
as far as possible.

9
00:01:48,702 --> 00:01:50,913
So it's modeled after a wolf howl, huh?

10
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:53,040
- [siren chirps]
- [exclaims, groans]

11
00:01:53,124 --> 00:01:54,166
[Haru chuckles]

12
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:59,588
And the star of the show
is this little stun gun, ah?

13
00:02:00,005 --> 00:02:01,799
Let's see here.

14
00:02:01,882 --> 00:02:05,261
I was told this will take down
anything that gets in your way.

15
00:02:05,344 --> 00:02:07,096
- [stun gun crackling]
- [exclaims]

16
00:02:07,596 --> 00:02:11,308
Yeah. I think it's sweet
you're so protective.

17
00:02:11,934 --> 00:02:13,769
But isn't this a bit much?

18
00:02:13,853 --> 00:02:15,229
Here's the thing.

19
00:02:15,312 --> 00:02:18,190
I have a feeling Melon's
not done with you yet.

20
00:02:18,274 --> 00:02:21,068
I'm not always gonna be
by your side to protect you.

21
00:02:21,152 --> 00:02:23,487
{\an8}I know how to take care of myself,
you know.

22
00:02:23,571 --> 00:02:25,114
You're not hearing me.

23
00:02:25,197 --> 00:02:27,616
If we were dealing with just some teacher,
that'd be fine.

24
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:30,411
But this is a killer with a grudge
against mixed couples.

25
00:02:30,494 --> 00:02:33,122
And he's definitely got some
anger issues with his parents.

26
00:02:33,205 --> 00:02:35,624
He's a serial devourer
and boss of the Shishi-Gumi--

27
00:02:35,708 --> 00:02:38,502
{\an8}He's the crazy guy who put
a few bullets in you. I get it.

28
00:02:38,586 --> 00:02:40,379
{\an8}Uh... Well, it's not about me.

29
00:02:40,462 --> 00:02:41,922
{\an8}This is about you.

30
00:02:42,631 --> 00:02:45,509
You didn't tell me anything
about what happened at school.

31
00:02:46,385 --> 00:02:47,845
And also, um...

32
00:02:48,929 --> 00:02:50,222
And also what?

33
00:02:50,598 --> 00:02:52,016
It's just that...

34
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:53,767
No, never mind.

35
00:02:54,059 --> 00:02:55,185
It's nothing.

36
00:02:55,269 --> 00:02:56,353
{\an8}Nothing?

37
00:02:56,812 --> 00:02:57,980
{\an8}You won't get mad?

38
00:02:58,063 --> 00:02:59,064
{\an8}I don't know.

39
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,566
[hesitatingly] Well...

40
00:03:01,275 --> 00:03:03,611
You and Melon, uh... Did...

41
00:03:03,694 --> 00:03:05,571
You didn't like him, right?

42
00:03:05,654 --> 00:03:06,864
Maybe just a little?

43
00:03:07,323 --> 00:03:08,532
- Huh?
- Uh...

44
00:03:08,616 --> 00:03:11,493
I mean, one day, I remember
you had Melon's scent on you.

45
00:03:11,577 --> 00:03:13,495
And even though you said
he was really shady,

46
00:03:13,579 --> 00:03:15,497
{\an8}you still made that promise with him,
so I was--

47
00:03:15,581 --> 00:03:16,582
{\an8}Legoshi!

48
00:03:16,832 --> 00:03:18,584
{\an8}That does make me mad!

49
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:21,295
{\an8}The only person
I'm interested in being with is you.

50
00:03:21,378 --> 00:03:22,588
{\an8}Huh?

51
00:03:22,671 --> 00:03:24,423
{\an8}- [chuckles]
- [scoffs] Really?

52
00:03:24,506 --> 00:03:26,842
- I'm glad this is so hilarious to you.
- [thuds]

53
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:29,345
Hey, there.

54
00:03:29,428 --> 00:03:31,138
- Hmm?
- Degoshi.

55
00:03:31,222 --> 00:03:32,431
So here's some bad news.

56
00:03:32,514 --> 00:03:33,807
You're suspected of murder.

57
00:03:33,891 --> 00:03:35,142
- Huh?
- What? Murder?

58
00:03:35,476 --> 00:03:38,062
They're about to put you on a wanted list.

59
00:03:38,145 --> 00:03:39,730
It'll be all over the news.

60
00:03:40,731 --> 00:03:43,234
You know, the tattoo parlor thing?

61
00:03:43,734 --> 00:03:45,569
"The tattoo parlor thing"?

62
00:03:45,736 --> 00:03:46,862
You've got it wrong.

63
00:03:46,946 --> 00:03:48,572
They were already dead when I got there.

64
00:03:48,656 --> 00:03:49,657
{\an8}What am I missing?

65
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:52,952
Well, the police want
to bust your hide ASAP.

66
00:03:53,035 --> 00:03:55,496
People get scared with stuff like this.

67
00:03:55,579 --> 00:03:58,165
As soon as your name drops,
here comes the press.

68
00:03:58,249 --> 00:04:01,543
Your story is gonna be
a popular search online.

69
00:04:01,627 --> 00:04:04,380
And unfortunately,
it won't matter if it's true or not.

70
00:04:04,463 --> 00:04:06,340
Well, I'm sure Mr. Yahya would underst--

71
00:04:06,423 --> 00:04:07,841
Understand?

72
00:04:07,925 --> 00:04:09,426
Are you sure about that?

73
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:12,596
Mm. Well, maybe not with that tone.

74
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:15,266
- You have devouring on your record, right?
- Huh?

75
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:19,144
If it were me on probation,
I'd steer clear of trouble.

76
00:04:19,228 --> 00:04:21,397
Wait a minute.
How do you know all of this?

77
00:04:21,939 --> 00:04:25,526
[Corn] I'm Intel Chief
of The 500 Cornered Rats.

78
00:04:25,609 --> 00:04:28,612
But at the end of the day,
you either listen or you don't.

79
00:04:28,696 --> 00:04:29,697
All right.

80
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,283
If you're ever in a bind,
just give me a call.

81
00:04:33,075 --> 00:04:35,703
You can try hiding,
but they will find you.

82
00:04:37,121 --> 00:04:40,124
Also, if you think you're
laying low, you're not.

83
00:04:41,166 --> 00:04:42,042
RATS

84
00:04:42,126 --> 00:04:43,335
[Haru] He seems serious.

85
00:04:43,669 --> 00:04:45,296
What are you thinking about?

86
00:04:45,379 --> 00:04:47,589
I don't have time to get arrested.

87
00:04:47,673 --> 00:04:49,508
Melon's still on the loose.

88
00:04:49,591 --> 00:04:51,468
[sighs] Is this even real?

89
00:04:51,885 --> 00:04:54,847
So does that mean you were
at the crime scene then?

90
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:57,933
Geez. Why did you even
go to that tattoo parlor?

91
00:04:58,017 --> 00:04:59,768
The last thing you'd do is get a tattoo.

92
00:04:59,852 --> 00:05:01,645
Well, it's Melon's go to studio, though.

93
00:05:01,729 --> 00:05:02,896
I thought it was a slam dunk.

94
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:06,775
I needed a lead and I thought I'd get it
from those tattoo guys.

95
00:05:06,859 --> 00:05:08,319
Hmm. That sounds--

96
00:05:08,402 --> 00:05:09,695
Uh, don't worry. Hold on.

97
00:05:09,778 --> 00:05:11,363
I didn't do anything dangerous.

98
00:05:11,447 --> 00:05:14,575
[sighs] You know what?
My school may have what you need.

99
00:05:14,658 --> 00:05:15,659
Huh?

100
00:05:15,743 --> 00:05:17,828
A lead on Melon or Professor Lumrong.

101
00:05:17,911 --> 00:05:19,204
Something might turn up.

102
00:05:19,288 --> 00:05:20,205
You're right!

103
00:05:20,289 --> 00:05:21,707
- Let's go!
- Wait! Ah!

104
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:23,250
Hang on. Hang on.

105
00:05:23,334 --> 00:05:25,002
- I'll go ask around.
- Huh?

106
00:05:25,085 --> 00:05:28,255
[Haru chuckles]
Hey, you'd stand out like a sore thumb.

107
00:05:30,841 --> 00:05:32,051
Hmm?

108
00:05:34,762 --> 00:05:36,638
{\an8}Uh, did you hear me?

109
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:38,307
{\an8}[Legoshi] Hmm.

110
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:39,475
{\an8}Legoshi?

111
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:41,101
You know...

112
00:05:41,769 --> 00:05:44,313
you're at a perfectly
kissable height right now.

113
00:05:44,396 --> 00:05:45,397
[Haru gasps]

114
00:05:45,481 --> 00:05:46,982
It just feels like...

115
00:05:47,441 --> 00:05:50,444
kissing you would be so natural
in this moment.

116
00:05:50,527 --> 00:05:53,238
I mean... now?

117
00:05:53,322 --> 00:05:55,407
I... I guess that's fine.

118
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:58,035
[whimsical music playing]

119
00:05:59,411 --> 00:06:00,454
[Haru sighs]

120
00:06:01,455 --> 00:06:03,665
Do you mind if we put this on hold?

121
00:06:03,749 --> 00:06:05,459
- On hold?
- [sighs]

122
00:06:05,542 --> 00:06:06,835
Here's the thing.

123
00:06:06,919 --> 00:06:08,462
Once I catch Melon,

124
00:06:08,545 --> 00:06:11,715
the Beastar is going to clear my record
of a devouring incident.

125
00:06:11,799 --> 00:06:12,841
[Haru] What?

126
00:06:12,925 --> 00:06:17,012
Then you and I won't have any problem
being together, officially.

127
00:06:17,805 --> 00:06:20,349
So maybe we put it on hold for now.

128
00:06:20,432 --> 00:06:21,934
- [chuckles]
- [Haru grumbles]

129
00:06:22,518 --> 00:06:23,769
{\an8}Oh, I get it.

130
00:06:24,228 --> 00:06:25,312
{\an8}On hold.

131
00:06:25,395 --> 00:06:27,606
{\an8}Aren't we a little full of ourselves?

132
00:06:29,108 --> 00:06:30,526
Haru? Wait, what did I say?

133
00:06:30,609 --> 00:06:31,902
Oh, nothing.

134
00:06:32,569 --> 00:06:34,363
[Legoshi] Come on!

135
00:06:34,488 --> 00:06:35,614
Haru!

136
00:06:38,033 --> 00:06:39,660
UDON BEBEBE

137
00:06:39,743 --> 00:06:44,039
We have reason to believe that the victim
got deliveries from your restaurant.

138
00:06:44,498 --> 00:06:46,708
Yeah. Something wrong with that?

139
00:06:46,792 --> 00:06:48,752
And he ordered from you often?

140
00:06:48,836 --> 00:06:52,631
Yep. I usually leave
all the delivery stuff to Legoshi.

141
00:06:52,714 --> 00:06:56,218
Did you find the various wounds
to his face or arms unusual?

142
00:06:56,301 --> 00:06:58,262
Well, the kid is a young wolf.

143
00:06:58,345 --> 00:07:00,139
A few scrapes really that big a deal?

144
00:07:00,222 --> 00:07:01,932
So you're saying that's normal?

145
00:07:02,057 --> 00:07:04,726
[stutters]
Oh, that's not what I meant by that.

146
00:07:06,395 --> 00:07:08,230
[Seven] Legoshi was always really nice.

147
00:07:08,313 --> 00:07:10,399
Just a normal kid to me.

148
00:07:10,649 --> 00:07:13,193
I guess you haven't heard
about his record of devouring?

149
00:07:13,485 --> 00:07:15,612
No, I never heard anything about that.

150
00:07:16,196 --> 00:07:19,324
[gasps] But when I think about it,
he always seemed very mindful.

151
00:07:19,408 --> 00:07:21,827
Like, careful never to touch an herbivore.

152
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:23,662
Hmm. Why do you think that is?

153
00:07:23,745 --> 00:07:26,748
I guess he just cared about
putting everyone's mind at ease.

154
00:07:26,832 --> 00:07:29,877
In other words, there was a possibility
he could hurt someone?

155
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,128
I don't think so.

156
00:07:31,211 --> 00:07:33,714
I haven't seen signs
of anything like that lately.

157
00:07:33,797 --> 00:07:35,257
So no recent examples

158
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:37,134
but that wasn't always the case?

159
00:07:38,010 --> 00:07:41,472
[sighs] Was he satisfying his hunger
with devourings?

160
00:07:42,055 --> 00:07:43,891
[suspenseful music playing]

161
00:08:06,413 --> 00:08:09,041
{\an8}[Louis] <i>Legoshi. He got set up again.</i>

162
00:08:09,124 --> 00:08:10,751
{\an8}LEGOSHI WANTED AS MURDER SUSPECT

163
00:08:10,834 --> 00:08:13,128
{\an8}<i>My guess is
Melon's misdirecting the police</i>

164
00:08:13,212 --> 00:08:15,047
{\an8}<i>so he can take down his next victim.</i>

165
00:08:15,839 --> 00:08:17,049
<i>What do I do?</i>

166
00:08:18,509 --> 00:08:21,178
[Peach] This was the Live Together
promotion office.

167
00:08:21,261 --> 00:08:24,139
[giggles] If you want to support us
and help stop prejudice

168
00:08:24,223 --> 00:08:26,391
against interspecies romance for good,

169
00:08:26,475 --> 00:08:29,311
just make sure you like and subscribe.

170
00:08:29,394 --> 00:08:31,313
Liv Together!

171
00:08:32,231 --> 00:08:33,815
- [beep]
- [cattle] And cut.

172
00:08:35,359 --> 00:08:36,818
- How was that?
- Good.

173
00:08:36,902 --> 00:08:38,779
{\an8}I think this one's gonna get some likes.

174
00:08:38,862 --> 00:08:40,614
{\an8}- Hopefully we can top 30.
- Yeah, no doubt.

175
00:08:40,697 --> 00:08:41,615
[Louis] Excuse me.

176
00:08:41,698 --> 00:08:43,492
{\an8}Whoa! Louis!

177
00:08:43,575 --> 00:08:44,993
Sorry to interrupt you all.

178
00:08:45,077 --> 00:08:46,078
{\an8}Oh! Oh! Let me guess.

179
00:08:46,161 --> 00:08:47,788
{\an8}You want to help with our mission, right?

180
00:08:47,871 --> 00:08:49,581
Uh... Yeah, maybe later.

181
00:08:49,665 --> 00:08:51,959
It's more about this string
of recent devourings.

182
00:08:52,042 --> 00:08:54,670
They seem to be aimed
at interspecies couples.

183
00:08:54,753 --> 00:08:57,839
The killer is very dangerous,
and he hasn't been caught yet.

184
00:08:57,923 --> 00:08:59,424
But I think you can help.

185
00:08:59,508 --> 00:09:02,761
Are you up for making a self-defense video
and posting it to your channel?

186
00:09:02,844 --> 00:09:05,222
Basically telling people
to watch their backs.

187
00:09:05,305 --> 00:09:06,515
Is that a good idea?

188
00:09:06,598 --> 00:09:08,767
I certainly understand your concerns.

189
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:11,812
But I don't want anyone else
to get caught up in these murders.

190
00:09:12,396 --> 00:09:14,565
You guys have a large following, right?

191
00:09:14,648 --> 00:09:16,400
Your videos get a lot of views.

192
00:09:16,775 --> 00:09:18,360
I think you could do some good.

193
00:09:18,443 --> 00:09:20,529
{\an8}- Well, what do you think?
- [bull] Mm.

194
00:09:20,946 --> 00:09:24,408
Well, since you're famous,
could we just use your name?

195
00:09:25,951 --> 00:09:27,661
You want to use my name?

196
00:09:28,912 --> 00:09:30,122
[cell phone buzzing]

197
00:09:30,205 --> 00:09:31,206
Huh?

198
00:09:31,665 --> 00:09:32,874
Excuse me.

199
00:09:34,543 --> 00:09:35,669
This is Louis.

200
00:09:35,752 --> 00:09:37,963
[Mayor on phone]
<i>Listen, where are you right now?</i>

201
00:09:38,046 --> 00:09:39,590
I'm at school. Why?

202
00:09:39,673 --> 00:09:41,133
<i>Do you see any press around?</i>

203
00:09:41,216 --> 00:09:42,342
<i>- Any police?</i>
- What?

204
00:09:43,427 --> 00:09:46,597
<i>I've been following the news
about your friend, the wanted one.</i>

205
00:09:47,306 --> 00:09:50,767
<i>I've pulled a few strings,
so the investigation steers clear of you.</i>

206
00:09:50,851 --> 00:09:52,728
I don't know what you mean by that.

207
00:09:52,978 --> 00:09:55,522
If it got out that the wolf
is your best friend,

208
00:09:55,606 --> 00:09:58,567
and on top of that,
you let that friend eat your leg?

209
00:09:58,650 --> 00:10:01,612
Guessing I don't have to tell you
what a problem that would be for us.

210
00:10:02,237 --> 00:10:03,447
<i>For the time being,</i>

211
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:05,907
<i>don't do any press, no interviews.</i>

212
00:10:05,991 --> 00:10:08,619
<i>Stay out of sight and behave yourself.</i>

213
00:10:08,702 --> 00:10:09,703
Got it?

214
00:10:09,786 --> 00:10:10,954
[line disconnects]

215
00:10:11,246 --> 00:10:12,456
[sighs wearily]

216
00:10:17,252 --> 00:10:19,504
So what do you think about our offer?

217
00:10:20,881 --> 00:10:22,633
You can go ahead and use my name.

218
00:10:22,716 --> 00:10:24,176
Yes! All right!

219
00:10:25,844 --> 00:10:27,012
[Bill] Nice to come together.

220
00:10:27,095 --> 00:10:28,138
- [Kibi] Yeah!
- [Bill] Nice.

221
00:10:28,221 --> 00:10:30,057
[Els] I think we're doing
pretty great so far.

222
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:32,225
- [Kibi] You know it.
- [Bill] Everyone is doing great.

223
00:10:32,601 --> 00:10:35,395
Doesn't it feel like Juno and Pena
are doing a lot better?

224
00:10:35,479 --> 00:10:37,856
{\an8}Totally. Who would have thought
they'd mesh so well?

225
00:10:37,939 --> 00:10:40,567
Yeah, those two were definitely
a challenge for us.

226
00:10:40,651 --> 00:10:42,152
- [Els chuckles]
- What? [gasps]

227
00:10:42,235 --> 00:10:43,445
[Els and Kibi gasp]

228
00:10:43,528 --> 00:10:46,865
DEVOURING CLUB
GO TO HELL

229
00:10:46,948 --> 00:10:47,908
This is terrible.

230
00:10:48,492 --> 00:10:51,203
It has to do with Legoshi, I think.

231
00:10:51,286 --> 00:10:53,455
He's not even a club member anymore.

232
00:10:53,538 --> 00:10:56,583
We didn't do anything
to deserve this kind of bullying.

233
00:10:56,667 --> 00:10:57,751
Unbelievable!

234
00:10:57,834 --> 00:10:59,628
Only cowards do this.

235
00:10:59,711 --> 00:11:01,463
Uh, to be fair,

236
00:11:01,546 --> 00:11:06,176
don't you all remember when we had to deal
with that devouring incident with Tim?

237
00:11:06,259 --> 00:11:09,930
And then there was Louis who got his leg
eaten so he could capture Riz.

238
00:11:10,013 --> 00:11:12,474
- Huh?
- Uh, we've had some drama in the club.

239
00:11:12,557 --> 00:11:14,726
Are you trying to put this on the seniors?

240
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:16,353
- That's not what I meant.
- [growls]

241
00:11:16,436 --> 00:11:17,437
[herbivores stammer]

242
00:11:18,105 --> 00:11:20,482
Well, now we all know what we have to do.

243
00:11:20,565 --> 00:11:22,401
We're amazing when we work together.

244
00:11:22,484 --> 00:11:25,112
When us carnivores
and herbivores work as a team,

245
00:11:25,195 --> 00:11:26,863
we can show whoever did this nonsense

246
00:11:26,947 --> 00:11:28,240
they made a big mistake.

247
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:30,909
- You're so cool.
- Yeah.

248
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:35,414
[Bill] <i>Still, I don't know what to believe
with this news about Legoshi.</i>

249
00:11:38,375 --> 00:11:39,918
[guard] Professor Lumrong?

250
00:11:40,001 --> 00:11:43,088
[Haru] Yeah, he left in
the middle of the semester, so...

251
00:11:43,171 --> 00:11:45,549
You don't know where he went
to work next, do you?

252
00:11:45,632 --> 00:11:47,592
I'd say forget about that.

253
00:11:47,676 --> 00:11:50,887
I went through his resume
and it was nothing but lies.

254
00:11:50,971 --> 00:11:53,056
Not a single thing on there matched up.

255
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:55,100
So no contact info I bet?

256
00:11:55,183 --> 00:11:56,560
Just more lies.

257
00:11:56,643 --> 00:11:57,978
If you ask me,

258
00:11:58,061 --> 00:12:00,230
they need thorough background checks.

259
00:12:00,730 --> 00:12:03,108
If you don't know
who you're really hiring,

260
00:12:03,191 --> 00:12:05,485
how is anyone supposed to feel safe?

261
00:12:05,569 --> 00:12:06,653
[sighs] Yeah.

262
00:12:07,487 --> 00:12:08,738
Thanks for all your help.

263
00:12:11,158 --> 00:12:12,200
[Haru grunts]

264
00:12:13,201 --> 00:12:14,411
[sighs]

265
00:12:14,494 --> 00:12:16,872
<i>Maybe the academic office knows something.</i>

266
00:12:16,955 --> 00:12:18,331
- [rustling]
<i>- Huh?</i>

267
00:12:18,415 --> 00:12:20,125
[rustling]

268
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:21,668
[suspenseful music playing]

269
00:12:27,549 --> 00:12:29,384
[whimpers softly]

270
00:12:32,804 --> 00:12:35,348
[sighing wearily]

271
00:12:36,516 --> 00:12:37,726
[sighing wearily]

272
00:12:38,226 --> 00:12:39,478
Oh, it's you.

273
00:12:39,561 --> 00:12:41,730
You're the one that
used to hang around Gohin.

274
00:12:41,813 --> 00:12:43,815
Yeah. You're the bamboo shop lady.

275
00:12:43,899 --> 00:12:46,234
Tell me how it feels
being so famous and such.

276
00:12:46,359 --> 00:12:47,360
Huh?

277
00:12:47,444 --> 00:12:49,488
All the reporters
are saying you're wanted.

278
00:12:49,571 --> 00:12:51,948
What? They're saying that I'm wanted?

279
00:12:52,032 --> 00:12:53,116
Yeah.

280
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,911
Huh. Here I thought you were
so young and carefree.

281
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:04,044
Well, I just, uh... Yeah.

282
00:13:04,628 --> 00:13:06,796
- Excuse me.
- Huh?

283
00:13:12,344 --> 00:13:15,096
[Legoshi] <i>I can't go to Gohin.
He doesn't deserve that.</i>

284
00:13:16,681 --> 00:13:17,641
RATS

285
00:13:17,724 --> 00:13:19,392
[sighs] <i>I guess I'll give it a shot.</i>

286
00:13:23,522 --> 00:13:24,523
Hmm.

287
00:13:27,901 --> 00:13:29,819
[sighs softly]

288
00:13:29,903 --> 00:13:32,405
RATS

289
00:13:40,789 --> 00:13:42,958
[water trickling]

290
00:14:01,351 --> 00:14:02,394
You're here.

291
00:14:04,271 --> 00:14:06,773
Seems like everything you said came true.

292
00:14:06,856 --> 00:14:08,900
I am definitely on the Most Wanted List.

293
00:14:09,484 --> 00:14:11,903
This had to have been
part of Melon's trap.

294
00:14:11,987 --> 00:14:13,029
A trap, huh?

295
00:14:13,446 --> 00:14:17,367
Well, I went over to the tattoo parlor
when I was trying to find Melon.

296
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:20,996
There were two dead bodies inside
and the police were instantly there.

297
00:14:21,079 --> 00:14:22,080
I see.

298
00:14:22,163 --> 00:14:23,415
[stomach growling]

299
00:14:23,498 --> 00:14:24,875
Oh. Uh...

300
00:14:24,958 --> 00:14:26,418
[laughs sheepishly]

301
00:14:26,501 --> 00:14:27,669
You're hungry, I guess.

302
00:14:27,752 --> 00:14:28,670
Huh?

303
00:14:29,045 --> 00:14:30,881
We have some meat for you to eat.

304
00:14:30,964 --> 00:14:32,841
No, thanks. I don't eat meat, actually.

305
00:14:32,924 --> 00:14:34,175
Don't be so picky.

306
00:14:34,259 --> 00:14:35,427
No, it's not about that.

307
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:36,803
Just eat it then.

308
00:14:36,887 --> 00:14:39,139
You don't know when
you'll eat again, Degoshi.

309
00:14:39,222 --> 00:14:41,808
Huh? My name's not Degoshi. It's Legoshi.

310
00:14:41,892 --> 00:14:44,311
Fugitives need to use an alias.

311
00:14:44,394 --> 00:14:45,562
That's like the same name.

312
00:14:45,645 --> 00:14:47,272
If you won't eat it, I will.

313
00:14:47,355 --> 00:14:49,774
Hey, stop! Stop, stop, stop! No fair!

314
00:14:49,858 --> 00:14:50,984
Give it back to me!

315
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:53,069
Do you guys really need to fight?

316
00:14:53,153 --> 00:14:55,614
I'm sure there's plenty of meat
around in the black market.

317
00:14:55,697 --> 00:14:57,949
Degoshi, meat is expensive.

318
00:14:58,033 --> 00:14:59,492
We can't always afford it.

319
00:14:59,576 --> 00:15:01,453
- Really?
- Remember this.

320
00:15:02,329 --> 00:15:05,832
The meat lined up in those stores
is reserved for business.

321
00:15:05,916 --> 00:15:10,795
Carnivores from mainstream society
will buy it, no matter what the price is.

322
00:15:10,879 --> 00:15:12,631
And the prices just keep rising.

323
00:15:13,173 --> 00:15:14,674
- Give it!
- [ICorn] Most carnivores

324
00:15:14,758 --> 00:15:17,886
living in the black market
don't have that kind of money.

325
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,973
That's why we the 500 cornered rats,

326
00:15:22,057 --> 00:15:26,102
were taking money from slime merchants
and distributing it to everyone.

327
00:15:26,186 --> 00:15:27,020
You like that?

328
00:15:27,103 --> 00:15:30,774
So that's why Mr. Corne
is cooperating with Mr. Yahya.

329
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:31,983
{\an8}Cooperating?

330
00:15:32,067 --> 00:15:33,193
{\an8}Not exactly.

331
00:15:33,276 --> 00:15:35,695
{\an8}Corne is nothing more
than a lapdog for the police.

332
00:15:35,779 --> 00:15:37,530
That sounds sort of insulting to dogs.

333
00:15:37,614 --> 00:15:39,574
{\an8}I say Yahya is the devil.

334
00:15:40,241 --> 00:15:42,827
And I can't stand that
they're working together.

335
00:15:42,911 --> 00:15:44,162
Outside the walls,

336
00:15:44,245 --> 00:15:48,041
those guys only make rules for themselves,
and carnivores get zero freedom.

337
00:15:48,124 --> 00:15:49,501
You think I'm wrong about that?

338
00:15:49,584 --> 00:15:50,835
Uh... Well...

339
00:15:51,586 --> 00:15:54,839
So carnivores come
to the black market to buy meat,

340
00:15:54,923 --> 00:15:56,508
and that way everyone's happy.

341
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,718
{\an8}Uh, yeah, I guess.

342
00:15:58,802 --> 00:16:02,973
Degoshi, didn't they frame you
for something that's not your fault?

343
00:16:03,056 --> 00:16:05,767
You can't trust creatures
who would do that to ya.

344
00:16:06,351 --> 00:16:09,938
The only good thing about herbivores
is how delicious their meat tastes.

345
00:16:10,021 --> 00:16:11,106
[both] So yummy!

346
00:16:11,189 --> 00:16:12,691
[Corn] All right. Time for bed.

347
00:16:12,774 --> 00:16:13,900
[both] Bedtime!

348
00:16:14,943 --> 00:16:16,194
[Legoshi] Hmm.

349
00:16:23,493 --> 00:16:27,872
<i>Never in my 18 years would I think
I'd find myself in a place like this.</i>

350
00:16:33,878 --> 00:16:36,840
CELEBRATING YOUR AWARD
CONGRATS ON THE GRAND PRIZE

351
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:38,258
[inhales]

352
00:16:39,801 --> 00:16:41,011
[exhales]

353
00:16:41,094 --> 00:16:42,679
- [cell phone ringing]
- Hmm?

354
00:16:44,305 --> 00:16:46,057
Oh. The chairman?

355
00:16:46,141 --> 00:16:46,975
OGMA

356
00:16:48,184 --> 00:16:51,646
Nepetalactol.
You figured out its molecular structure.

357
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:55,567
The active compound found in catnip.
And you synthesized it?

358
00:16:56,109 --> 00:16:57,318
Fantastic.

359
00:16:57,402 --> 00:16:59,029
I appreciate you saying that, sir.

360
00:16:59,404 --> 00:17:01,364
Applying this to feline attractants,

361
00:17:01,448 --> 00:17:02,907
this could be revolutionary.

362
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,827
It seems you're quite gifted.

363
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:07,829
Which brings me to my request.

364
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,794
We're having a production issue
with a certain project.

365
00:17:14,878 --> 00:17:16,296
There's a stability problem.

366
00:17:19,132 --> 00:17:22,510
This looks like some kind of
nutritional supplement?

367
00:17:22,927 --> 00:17:25,638
We're experimenting with artificial meat.

368
00:17:25,722 --> 00:17:27,015
Oh, I see.

369
00:17:27,932 --> 00:17:31,519
I'd like you to work closely with
Ogura Foods on its development.

370
00:17:31,895 --> 00:17:33,563
With Ogura Foods?

371
00:17:34,397 --> 00:17:36,816
Ah! Because Louis is going to marry...

372
00:17:37,776 --> 00:17:39,903
I mean...

373
00:17:39,986 --> 00:17:43,114
I'm not good
at, uh, collaborative research.

374
00:17:43,198 --> 00:17:45,033
We'll provide the necessary funding.

375
00:17:45,116 --> 00:17:46,659
Consider it a blank check.

376
00:17:47,410 --> 00:17:50,455
In addition, we'll prepare a private lab
solely for your use.

377
00:17:51,372 --> 00:17:53,124
This is the executive key.

378
00:17:53,541 --> 00:17:55,794
You're welcome to it any day, anytime.

379
00:17:56,586 --> 00:17:57,962
Hmm.

380
00:17:58,463 --> 00:17:59,756
You're not impressed.

381
00:18:00,465 --> 00:18:01,633
Very well.

382
00:18:01,716 --> 00:18:03,551
We'll throw in lounge access, too.

383
00:18:03,635 --> 00:18:05,136
[chuckles]

384
00:18:05,637 --> 00:18:06,805
Well, that sounds nice.

385
00:18:06,888 --> 00:18:10,225
Our delivery expectation
is by the third quarter.

386
00:18:10,308 --> 00:18:11,309
Yes, sir.

387
00:18:12,602 --> 00:18:16,147
If I may, uh,
about the artificial meat project,

388
00:18:16,231 --> 00:18:18,942
{\an8}where are we in terms of its development?

389
00:18:19,025 --> 00:18:20,860
Don't hover above your pay grade.

390
00:18:20,944 --> 00:18:22,821
Uh... Yes, sir.

391
00:18:23,571 --> 00:18:26,157
It'll be our trump card
for the Zoolympic bid.

392
00:18:26,741 --> 00:18:29,285
We need this done well and on time.

393
00:18:29,702 --> 00:18:32,205
I'll be sure and give it my best.
Thank you, sir.

394
00:18:35,208 --> 00:18:37,710
Arranged marriages,
since you mentioned it,

395
00:18:37,794 --> 00:18:39,045
are an effective means

396
00:18:39,129 --> 00:18:43,967
of bringing us together and forging
rather important political alliances.

397
00:18:44,050 --> 00:18:45,093
[sighs]

398
00:18:45,677 --> 00:18:50,098
Well, I'm certainly no expert, sir,
but when it comes to procreation,

399
00:18:50,181 --> 00:18:54,727
the amount of testosterone that's produced
by the male is an important factor.

400
00:18:56,729 --> 00:18:58,189
Excuse me, sir.

401
00:19:04,028 --> 00:19:05,238
[door closes echoes]

402
00:19:06,823 --> 00:19:08,575
[reporter speaking on radio]

403
00:19:08,658 --> 00:19:11,286
[reporter] <i>...an employee and a customer
were found in the scene</i>

404
00:19:11,369 --> 00:19:14,414
<i>inside the second-generation
Seiryu Tattoo Studio</i>

405
00:19:14,497 --> 00:19:16,499
<i>in the First Ocean District.</i>

406
00:19:16,583 --> 00:19:20,503
<i>Police discovered a large quantity
of the recently banned energy drink Kines</i>

407
00:19:20,587 --> 00:19:22,922
<i>in the apartment
of the suspected wolf at large Legoshi.</i>

408
00:19:23,006 --> 00:19:24,632
- What?
<i>- Any information regarding...</i>

409
00:19:24,716 --> 00:19:26,634
There's no way they found that in my room.

410
00:19:26,718 --> 00:19:28,678
[man 1] <i>Empty Kenis cans were also found</i>

411
00:19:28,761 --> 00:19:31,848
<i>at the scene of the interspecies
murder cases, weren't they?</i>

412
00:19:31,931 --> 00:19:33,933
[man 2] <i>Yes, it's natural to think that</i>

413
00:19:34,017 --> 00:19:37,228
<i>the unsolved serial-devouring incidents
may be related.</i>

414
00:19:37,312 --> 00:19:40,023
<i>It's possible Legoshi
was also behind these crimes.</i>

415
00:19:40,106 --> 00:19:41,941
[man 1] <i>So what's his motive here?</i>

416
00:19:42,025 --> 00:19:45,987
[man 2] <i>Well, making carnivores drink
Kenis is to get them to kill herbivores,</i>

417
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:48,823
<i>then killing those attacking carnivores?</i>

418
00:19:48,907 --> 00:19:51,367
<i>What a heinous beast, if you ask me.</i>

419
00:19:51,784 --> 00:19:55,079
- [man 1] <i>If we don't catch him soon...
-</i> [man 2] <i>...then his killing spree</i>

420
00:19:55,163 --> 00:19:56,372
<i>- will continue.</i>
- [man 1] <i>Right.</i>

421
00:19:56,456 --> 00:19:59,125
[man 2] <i>The faster we find
this deadly gray wolf, the better.</i>

422
00:19:59,209 --> 00:20:01,336
[reporter]
<i>We appreciate your input, gentlemen.</i>

423
00:20:01,419 --> 00:20:03,296
<i>Next up is the weather forecast.</i>

424
00:20:04,172 --> 00:20:07,300
[sighs] This is such a mess.

425
00:20:07,383 --> 00:20:09,510
Degoshi, congratulations.

426
00:20:09,594 --> 00:20:11,888
You're the most dangerous carnivore
in the whole world.

427
00:20:11,971 --> 00:20:14,599
There's nothing funny about this.
Seriously.

428
00:20:14,682 --> 00:20:18,353
Well, it looks like you'll have to hide
out here until the heat dies down.

429
00:20:18,895 --> 00:20:20,021
[Legoshi sighs]

430
00:20:21,689 --> 00:20:23,441
[Legoshi] I wonder if Haru is all right.

431
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:30,823
- [girl] Haru!
- Huh?

432
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:33,326
Tell me you've seen this.

433
00:20:33,409 --> 00:20:34,619
Is this true?

434
00:20:34,702 --> 00:20:35,703
{\an8}LEGOSHI WANTED FOR MURDER

435
00:20:35,787 --> 00:20:39,249
{\an8}- No. Don't believe everything you read.
- So scary. Are you okay, Haru?

436
00:20:39,916 --> 00:20:42,210
This is even worse than Ako's boyfriend.

437
00:20:42,293 --> 00:20:44,254
Well, he said it's a false accusation.

438
00:20:44,337 --> 00:20:47,799
Wait. So, like, you believe
what your boyfriend says?

439
00:20:48,132 --> 00:20:49,926
That's true love. [laughs]

440
00:20:51,135 --> 00:20:52,470
What are you thinking?

441
00:20:52,887 --> 00:20:56,599
Well, I just have this feeling
like someone's watching me.

442
00:20:56,975 --> 00:20:59,227
Uh-oh. Maybe it's your boyfriend.

443
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:03,690
But wait, aren't you the one who's always
saying you can protect yourself?

444
00:21:03,773 --> 00:21:06,526
[Haru]
<i>After 19 years as a rabbit, I get it.</i>

445
00:21:08,027 --> 00:21:11,281
<i>No matter how much I act tough
about protecting myself,</i>

446
00:21:11,823 --> 00:21:17,161
<i>if someone stands behind me, it's scary,
because I know I could never win.</i>

447
00:21:17,245 --> 00:21:19,414
[tense music playing]

448
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:23,960
[footsteps approaching]

449
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:29,632
[Haru breathing shakily]

450
00:21:30,758 --> 00:21:33,011
[footsteps approaching, stops]

451
00:21:34,012 --> 00:21:35,013
Uh...

452
00:21:36,264 --> 00:21:37,682
[footsteps continue approaching]

453
00:21:37,765 --> 00:21:39,058
[panting]

454
00:21:39,642 --> 00:21:41,019
[footsteps stop]

455
00:21:48,192 --> 00:21:49,110
[Haru grunts]

456
00:21:49,193 --> 00:21:52,113
- [stun gun crackling]
- [groaning]

457
00:21:52,488 --> 00:21:53,448
[Haru panting]

458
00:21:55,783 --> 00:22:00,455
[groaning]

459
00:22:01,122 --> 00:22:03,124
[closing theme song playing]
